{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "description": "Protected brands for app/analysis/impersonation.py. Each entry names an app that fraudsters clone; the module flags APKs that wear a brand's package name, display name, or icon without being that brand's app.",
  "status": "15 of 66 brands carry a signing certificate read from a real APK, so the certificate check runs for them; 6 also carry a launcher icon hash. The remainder are package/label entries verified against a live store listing.",
  "how_to_extend": "Do not hand-write icon_phash or cert_sha256 — both must come from a genuine APK obtained from the official listing, which is what scripts/build_brand_reference.py does. Adding a brand by package name alone still powers the typosquat and label checks.",
  "warning": "A WRONG package name here creates a false positive on the real app: the genuine bank APK would read as a typosquat of a package that does not exist. Verify each entry against the official store listing before relying on this table in a deployment. SECOND RULE, equally load-bearing: once a brand has ANY cert_sha256 recorded, EVERY package listed under it is certificate-checked against that list, so a package whose own signing key has not been recorded will make the genuine app on it read as a clone. Only list packages you have verified.",
